Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:49:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Align frozen-runner qualification fixtures

Base: 30e56e093b33a9f45d6f58d032d65ed5055a2105 (tree c3a9bf4be9b672f11c99f0c3098778a901dbae99).

Rationale: port the existing candidate-38 test-only corrections 0685, 0686 and 0687 to the storage qualification harness. Stand-in runners/workers must expose the methods and fields the frozen runtime reads. Native-memory accounting uses a controlled free-memory input while real CUDA allocation and graph cleanup still run.

Quality: no runtime source or arithmetic changes; assertions are retained and the native accounting assertion becomes exact. These files are mounted only in test containers.

Tests: all three original patches apply cleanly to a fresh canonical source worktree. GB10 rerun is pending; retain the original failed gate.

Upstream status: local qualification fixtures for the LIL source; reused from the repository test fixes, not a serving change.
